[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: TC-H1FHI-
TITLE: Test Protocol

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-22
TITLE: Collimator
STATEMENT: >>>
The service user should be able to check the reported ID of the attached collimator and if it’s disconnected the reported ID should be 0
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The user should be service user

2. The system should be powered on without any collimator connected to it.

3. The system should be in service mode
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. the collimator should be disconnected by service user

2. power on the system

3. Check The head interface board

4. Connect the collimator

5. Check The head interface board
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the collimator is disconnected

2. Verify system is ready to use and there is no treatment plan is loaded to the system.

3. Verify the reported ID is 0 for the collimator

4. Verify collimator is connected

5. Verify the reported ID is updated accordingly with the connected collimator
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-9
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-14
TITLE: Collimator Interlock - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When user applies fake emissions (e.g. fake HVPS) to the system and remove Collimator verify head interface interlock fault.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1.The system is ready to run.

2.A fake emission should be simulated for the plan (e.g. fake HVPS)

3.A 20 second treatment plan should be ready to load and run.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1.Power on the system with modified no emission output (e.g. fake HVPS).

2.Load a 20 second treatment plan.

3.Start the emission for 5 seconds.

4.Remove the collimator.
5.Check the fault.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1.Verify the system is up and ready to run.

2.Verify the plan is loaded successfully.

3.Verify the emission is started.

4.Verify physically that the collimator is removed.

5.Verify head interface interlock fault displayed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-2
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-17
TITLE: Illumination LEDs 1 - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When user press and release the laser membrane key several times, verify the head interface firmware should enable / disable the head
lasers.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1.System is ready to run.

2.No treatment plan is running.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1.Check the system when is powered on.

2.Press membrane key.

3.Check the head lasers.

4.Press membrane key again.

5.Check the head lasers.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify there is no treatment.

2. Verify physically that the membrane key is pressed.

3. Verify it’s disabled.

4. Verify physically that the membrane key is pressed.

5. Verify it’s enabled.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-5
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-25
TITLE: Cooling system flow
STATEMENT: >>>
The service user should be able to view system flow values in the services screen.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The user should be service user

2. The system should be powered on without any treatment plan loaded.

3. The system should be in service mode

4. There should be a treatment plan ready to load into the system.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. The head interface firmware shall be able to read and convert a PWM feedback signal for monitoring the cooling system’s flow sensor
readings
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify firmware can read and convert a PWM feedback signal for monitoring the cooling system’s flow sensor readings
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-12
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-24
TITLE: Membrane key switches
STATEMENT: >>>
Service user should verify that he / she could view the membrane key state values in the service screen. Note that there are 5 individual
switches.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The user should be service user

2. The system should be powered on without any treatment plan loaded.

3. The system should be in service mode
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Check the system when is powered on

2. Click Service symbol in the left panel of the screen

3. Check the services screen

4. One by one press and release the membrane key switches. Notice that there are 5 switches.

5. Check the services screen
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is ready to use and there is no treatment plan is loaded.

2. Verify the services screen displayed

3. Verify the membrane key state values. Make a note of the values

4. Verify user can do it without any issues.

5. Verify the membrane key state values. Make a note of the values
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-11
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-54
TITLE: Membrane key switches
STATEMENT: >>>
The service user should be able to check the reported ID of the attached QC collimator and report QC Diode data
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The user should be service user

2. The system should be powered on without any collimator connected to it.

3. The system should be in service mode
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. The QC collimator should be connected by service user

2. Check the head interface board

3. Run a QC procedure

4. Check the QC Diode readings
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the collimator is connected

2. Verify system is ready to use and there is QC data below the low threshold

3. Verify the QC procedure begins

4. Verify the QC reading increases significantly when the QC procedure is running
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-53
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-19
TITLE: Cooling System Temperature
STATEMENT: >>>
When a service user power on the system without loading any treatment plan, he/she be able to see the water temperature on GUI.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is stable and ready to run

2. User has to be a service user.

3. The system should be in service mode
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Service user should Power on the system

2. Click the Service symbol in the left panel of the screen
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is powered on and is in a stable mode and ready to run. Also, verify there isn’t any treatment plan loaded in the system

2. Verify the temperature of the water which should be between 10C and 40C.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-1
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-23
TITLE: Magnetometers readings
STATEMENT: >>>
The service user can view each magnetometer feedback reporting data in the service screen which has to be NON-zero ones.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The user should be service user

2. The system should be powered on without any collimator connected to it.

3. The system should be in service mode

4. There is no treatment plan loaded into system
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Power on the system

2. Click services symbol in the left-hand side panel

3. Check the service screen
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system powered on successfully without any treatment plan loaded on.

2. Verify the service screen displayed in the GUI

3. Verify each magnetometer feedback reporting data on screen is displayed which has to be non-zero.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-10
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-21
TITLE: Main Board Communication
STATEMENT: >>>
The user has to check the head interface board to verify its communication with Main Board and sending the values to Main board at a rate
greater than 1Hz.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The system is ready to run.

2. The user be able to check LED on the Main board

3. The User be able to check the head interface for sending values to main board
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Check the system when is powered on

2. Check The head interface board

3. Check the mainboard LED TBD
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is ready to use.

2. Verify it send values to Main board periodically

3. Verify it’s pulsing at a rate much faster than 1 Hz
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-8
  ROLE: Verifies

