[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-16
TITLE: Cooling System Pressure - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
When a service user powers on the system and checks the service screen, he/she should view pressure values before and after the loading
the treatment plan.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1.The system should be powered on and ready to use.

2.The user should be service user.

3.A plan should be ready to load and run.

4.The system should be in service mode.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Start the system with power on.

2. Click Service symbol in the left panel.

3. Check system pressure values.

4. Load a treatment plan.

5. Start the treatment.

6. Click Service symbol in the left panel.

7. Check system pressure values.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the system is on and no treatment plan is loaded.

2. Verify the services displayed in the GUI.

3. Verify it’s below 1 psi.

4. Verify the plan is loaded successfully.

5. Verify the treatment started.

6. Verify the services displayed in the GUI.

7. Verify it’s above 1 psi.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-13
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FHI-56
TITLE: Robot Hand Guidance Button Test
STATEMENT: >>>
Service user should verify that the robot arm moves in manually guided positions when the button is pressed down and holds its position
upon release.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
1. The user should be service user

2. The system should be powered on

3. The robot arm should be ready and in a safe, reachable position to move
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Check the system is powered on

2. Check the robot status LED and robot controller to ensure arm is ready for hand guidance

3. If the button is not safely reachable, use the GUI to change the arm to the “Treatment” position

4. With one hand holding the opposite side of the treatment hand, and the other holding the bar with the manual guidance button, press and
hold the button down

5. Gently push the robot arm in all 6 directions: forward, backward, left, right, up, and down, within comfortable reach

6. Release the robot hand guidance button
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. The system should appear in normal operation with no interlocks or errors tripped.

2. The system should be on, and the robot arm LED should be flashing blue

3. The robot arm moves to the treatment position with no issues. The head can be reached.

4. The robot arm should have a relay that has an audible click once the button is engaged. The LEDs on the robot arm should change color.
The robot arm should respond to the button press in under 1 second.

5. The robot arm should move in all directions smoothly without interruption.

6. The robot arm relay should have an audible click again. The LED’s on the robot arm return to the ready state color. The robot arm holds
its position within 1 second of the button’s release. The robot arm is immovable with the same pressure applied in Step 5.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FHI-55
  ROLE: Verifies

[[/SECTION]]
